{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 1, :comments ["<b>This is the book of the generations of Adam.</b> That even the reading-marker of the book, the Holy One, blessed be He, gave to the first Adam. And in Torat Kohanim it concludes: ואהבת לרעך כמוך — Rabbi Akiva said: this is a great principle in the Torah. Ben Azzai says: זה ספר תולדות אדם is greater. The explanation: it stands on the conclusion of the verse, בדמות אלהים עשה אותו, for from the verse of Rabbi Akiva we only hear that what is hateful to you do not do to your fellow, and Ben Azzai comes and says that even if he is not concerned for his own honor, he must be concerned for his fellow's honor, because he sees his fellow's likeness but does not see his own likeness, and therefore he said that this verse includes more than the verse ואהבת לרעך כמוך."], :book :genesis, :voice :daat-zkenim, :lang :en, :chapter 5, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:05:04.581431667Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}